Jeff will pick a card at random from ten cards numbered 1 through X.  The number on this card will indicate his starting point on the number line shown below.  He will then spin the fair spinner shown below (which has three congruent sectors) and follow the instruction indicated by his spin.  From this new point he will spin the spinner again and follow the resulting instruction.  What is the probability that he ends up at a multiple of 3 on the number line?  Express your answer as a common fraction. [asy]
import graph;
size(10cm);
defaultpen(linewidth(0.7)+fontsize(8));

xaxis(-2,13,Ticks(OmitFormat(-1),1.0,begin=false,end=false,beginlabel=false,endlabel=false),Arrows(4));

label("-1",(-1,-0.98));

real r=3.5;
pair center=(17,0);
draw(circle(center,r));
int i;
for(i=1;i<=3;++i)

{

draw(center--center+r*dir(120*i-30));

}
label("$\parbox{1cm}{move \\ 1 space \\ left}$",center+r/2*dir(150));
label("$\parbox{1cm}{move \\ 1 space \\ right}$",center+r/2*dir(270));
label("$\parbox{1cm}{move \\ 1 space \\ right}$",center+r/2*dir(30));
draw(center--center+3*r/4*dir(80), The angle of the arrow is 90 degrees. What is the value of unknown variable X?

