Using polynomial long division, we have
$$\begin{array}{c|ccccc}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{x^3} & +3x^2 & + 9x & + 28 \\
\cline{2-6}
x-3 & x^4 & & & +x & + 2 \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{x^4} & -3x^3 & & & \\
\cline{2-3}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{0} & 3x^3 & & & \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & 3x^3 & -9x^2 & & \\
\cline{3-4}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & 0 & 9x^2 & + x & \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & 9x^2 & - 27x & \\
\cline{4-5}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & 0 & 28x & + 2 \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & & 28x & - 84 \\
\cline{5-6}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & & 0 & 86 \\
\end{array}$$
Therefore, the remainder is $\boxed{86}$.
The answer is: 86

