A counter-clockwise rotation by $120^\circ$ about the origin can be represented by the matrix \[
\begin{pmatrix}
\cos 120^\circ & -\sin 120^\circ \\
\sin 120^\circ & \cos 120^\circ
\end{pmatrix}
= \begin{pmatrix}
-1/2 & -\sqrt{3}/2 \\
\sqrt{3}/2 & -1/2
\end{pmatrix}.
